From f12deb79d7d6d1075395acffa093b3a58f987bd1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <zenithblue.dev@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:29:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] panvk: v9+ unlowered fragment shader while the depth
 bounds test is off

Rationale: perf review 2026-10-26 finding C1 (c-gpu.md). Since csf-v11
092/116 (v10+) and jm-v9 018 (v9), a fragment shader compiled while the
depth bounds enable may be dynamic, or without pipeline state, carries
the emulation (panvk_lower_depth_bounds()). It always writes SampleMask,
so the shader has writes_coverage and no FPK, the ZS update is forced
late with depth writes or an occlusion query, and fs_required() is true
even with every color write masked. DXVK reports depthBounds on the X6
and compiles its fragment shader libraries with the enable dynamic, and
D3D11 never turns the test on, so every draw on a fast-linked pipeline
paid for a test that was never enabled. jm-v7 076 fixed this on v6/v7
with an unlowered alternate compile picked per draw; this ports its FS
half to v9+.

- panvk_shader::alt/alt_parent, the alternate compile and its nested
  [de]serialization are no longer v6/v7-only. On v9+ only fragment
  shaders get one (panvk_db_alt_wanted(), also used by v6/v7's
  panvk_v7_wants_alt(), whose result is unchanged); 077's xfb VS stays
  v6/v7.
- cmd_select_db_alt_fs() picks the compile at the start of each CSF
  draw and v9 JM draw layer, before fs.required: the lowered one while
  the test is on and a depth attachment is bound (the db_on of
  build_dcd_flags(), of the v9 JM DCD and of the ds.enable sysval), the
  unlowered one otherwise. A change marks FS and FS_PUSH_UNIFORMS dirty,
  so FS registers, descriptors, push uniforms, blend, ZSD, DCD and tiler
  flags follow. Rebinding the main compile while its alternate is in the
  state is not a change (jm-v7 098, now on every arch).
- panvk_hash_state() hashes whether the FS carries the alternate, so a
  pipeline with a dynamic enable never gets a cached binary without it
  (a static enable hashes the same depth_bounds bit), and a
  PANVK_DB_ALT=0 run never gets one with it. The serialized format
  changes on v9+; the cache and shader binary UUIDs include the driver
  build-id, so no 114 blob is read.

Cost: those fragment shaders are compiled twice and their binaries take
twice the memory (as with 076 on v6/v7). Sharing the front end (the late
clone of perf-review-2026-10-22 item 8) is left for later.

Knobs: PANVK_DB_ALT=0 = 114 on v9+ (only the lowered FS is compiled and
drawn). Default on.
Arch: v9+ (CSF v10+ and v9 JM); v6/v7 behaviour is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
